  the animated shot starts with a true  aerial shot and the only camera movement  we see is a slow pan from above  then more birds appear because more  birds simply appear before the camera  lives no different they are both  wonderful shots yeah but it's not easy  now here's our first major departure we  have this shot of zebras going wild  jumping up on two legs  we don't really see this in the original  until much later it's not until baby  Simba is presented that we see something  comparable and it's still not quite the  same alright 5-row be careful because  you're messing with our childhoods don't  do that again next up is the slow and  gorgeous zoom to reveal Pride Rock in  the new version in the original the shot  is much longer and the zoom is much much  faster in 1994 the shot tracked Zazu all  the way up to Pride Rock and we see a  prideful Mufasa standing atop it in the  2019 version we only see a little bitty  Mufasa  but perhaps Disney is only giving us a  snippet in the teaser and the shot  actually continues on in the movie  everybody's ok with this did I miss  something now it's time to meet Rafiki  his climb up the rocks seems about right  but in the original Rafiki is first  revealed walking through a crowd of  animals again who can say how it will  happen in the 2019 version Rafiki also  just looks nicer in the 1994 version you  wrote some fossa in with a friendly hug  and I'm just seeing less personality  this time around peculiar don't you  think alright here we go this is the  biggest difference we all know that read  swipe that essentially annoyed Simba as  a successor to his Father's throne well  in the original Rafiki cracks open some  type of fruit the jury is still out on  exactly what type of food it was someone  line are saying it's a passion fruit  others are saying that it's a  pomegranate I don't really know what it  is I just know that it's juicy and I  would eat it what I wouldn't eat are  those dry red sticks that Rafiki uses in  t