here to  dissect in the new version there's a  scene where Simba puts his paw in a  bigger paw print in the original this  moment comes when Simba and Mufasa are  having a serious conversation about  bravery and the new version it seems  like the paw print is a little bit  smaller last there's a quick shot of  what I assume is the Stampede scene  there pretty darn similar there's a bit  more green grass and the terrain is a  tad more dramatic in  original okay what's really last is what  we hear during the teaser actor James  Earl Jones reprising his role as Mufasa  says everything the light touches is our  kingdom  yada yada yeah I mean it's the same  actor saying it so it's no surprise that  it's spot-on but listen to both lines in  both versions everything the light  touches is our kingdom everything the  light touches is our kingdom they're  practically the same line reading but  that's where the differences come in  Simba says after that first line we  don't hear that in the teaser instead we  hear the word but but Aki's time is  ruler rises and falls like the Sun  there's no but in the original a king's  time as ruler rises and falls like the  Sun then in the original he goes on to  say one day Simba the Sun will set on my  time here and will rise with you as the  new king in the new teaser Jones doesn't  say the word Simba perhaps these words  were added or taken away just for the  teaser we won't know for sure until the  movie comes out in 2019 all right there  you have it what did I miss  was I wrong about anything tell us in  the comments  [Music]

